Subject: [PATCH] cal: fix -Wextra sign-compare

day is read from the int day-array through an unsigned pointer,
with -1 (SPACE) sentinels - compare against (unsigned)SPACE to
keep the exact promoted semantics.
diff --git a/util-linux/cal.c b/util-linux/cal.c
index 522ab34..067a93d 100644
--- a/util-linux/cal.c
+++ b/util-linux/cal.c
@@ -347,7 +347,7 @@ static char *build_row(char *p, unsigned *dp)
 	col = 0;
 	do {
 		day = *dp++;
-		if (day != SPACE) {
+		if (day != (unsigned)SPACE) {
 			if (julian) {
 				++p;
 				if (day >= 100) {
